#### Technical Notes

**Proposed README Structure** (add after "Animation Techniques" section):

```markdown
## Dynamic Text Feature

**NEW**: Selected animations now support custom text input, allowing you to generate personalized animations with your own words and fonts!

### Supported Animation Types

**9 unique animation styles across 15 animation files** (83% coverage):

**SVG Path-Based** (6 animations):
- ✅ Universal Paths - Entrance animation showcase
- ✅ Glitch - Digital corruption effects
- ✅ 3D Transforms - Perspective and depth
- ✅ Reveal/Mask - Sliding mask reveals
- ✅ Wave/Ripple - Fluid wave distortions
- ✅ Typewriter - Sequential character typing

**Particle-Based** (3 animations):
- ✅ Particles - Canvas pixel sampling
  - Base: Standard particle system
  - Varied: Different particle behaviors
  - Procedural: Randomized generation

**Liquid/Blob** (3 animations):
- ✅ Liquid/Blobs - Circle packing in letter shapes
  - Base: Metaball coalescing
  - Varied: Different blob behaviors
  - Procedural: Randomized blob patterns

**Morphing** (3 animations):
- ✅ Morphing - Shape interpolation with flubber.js
  - Base: Circle to letter morphing
  - Varied: Different start shapes
  - Procedural: Random shape generation

**Not Yet Supported**:
- ⏸️ Line Drawing (3 animations) - Requires stroke extraction (complex)

### How to Use

1. Open the gallery (`index.html` in a browser)
2. Scroll to an animation card with the editor panel (look for font picker and text input)
3. **Select a font** from the dropdown (8 fonts available)
4. **Enter your custom text** in the text input field (max 100 characters)
5. Click the **"✨ Generate"** button
6. Watch your text come alive with the selected animation!

**Tips**:
- Use short, impactful phrases for best results ("DO MORE", "GO BIG", etc.)
- Different fonts create dramatically different visual styles
- Try the same text across multiple animation types
- Multi-word text creates stacked layouts in most animations

### Available Fonts

| Font | Style | Best For |
|------|-------|----------|
| **Anton** | Bold sans-serif | Strong, impactful messages |
| **Roboto Bold** | Modern sans-serif | Clean, professional text |
| **Oswald Bold** | Condensed sans-serif | Tall, narrow layouts |
| **Bangers** | Comic/display | Fun, energetic vibes |
| **Bungee** | Layered display | Retro, bold statements |
| **Black Ops One** | Stencil military | Edgy, tactical themes |
| **Permanent Marker** | Hand-drawn | Casual, handwritten feel |
| **Press Start 2P** | 8-bit pixel | Retro gaming nostalgia |

All fonts are open-source and loaded from `/fonts/` directory.

### Technical Architecture

The dynamic text system uses several modern web technologies:

**Text-to-Path Conversion**:
- **opentype.js** - Parses TrueType fonts (.ttf) and converts text to SVG path data
- Each letter becomes a `<path>` element with precise vector outlines
- Supports arbitrary fonts and text without pre-rendering

**Animation-Specific Processing**:
- **SVG Path animations** - Use raw path data from opentype.js
- **Particle animations** - Render text to canvas, sample pixels for particle positions
- **Liquid animations** - Pack circles inside letter shapes using point-in-polygon tests
- **Morphing animations** - Use flubber.js to smoothly interpolate between shapes

**Gallery ↔ Animation Communication**:
- **postMessage API** - Secure cross-iframe messaging
- **Origin validation** - Only accepts messages from same origin (prevents XSS)
- Two message types:
  - `updateTextPaths` - SVG path data for path-based animations
  - `updateText` - Raw text + font for canvas-based animations

**Libraries Used**:
- [opentype.js](https://opentype.js.org/) (v1.3.4) - Font parsing
- [flubber.js](https://github.com/veltman/flubber) (v0.4.2) - Path morphing
- Canvas API - Pixel sampling for particles
- SVG - Vector rendering and animation

### Troubleshooting

**Problem**: Font doesn't load / "Font not loaded" error

**Solutions**:
- Check browser console for specific error messages
- Verify font files exist in `/fonts/` directory
- Ensure font files are valid TrueType (.ttf) format
- Try a different font - some may fail to load due to file corruption
- Hard refresh the page (Cmd+Shift+R / Ctrl+Shift+R)

---

**Problem**: Text looks wrong or doesn't render

**Solutions**:
- Some fonts may not support all special characters
- Stick to alphanumeric characters (A-Z, 0-9) for best compatibility
- Avoid emojis and complex Unicode characters
- Try a simpler font (Anton, Roboto) if issues persist

---

**Problem**: Text is cut off or too small

**Solutions**:
- Text is rendered with fixed viewBox dimensions (700x280)
- Very long text may overflow - keep phrases short (< 20 characters recommended)
- Use 1-3 words for optimal visual impact
- Multi-word text automatically stacks vertically

---

**Problem**: Animation doesn't update after clicking "Generate"

**Solutions**:
- Refresh the page and try again
- Ensure browser JavaScript is enabled
- Check browser console for errors
- Try a different animation type (some may have issues)
- Wait a few seconds - generation may take time for complex text

---

**Problem**: Multiple clicks don't work

**Solutions**:
- Wait for previous generation to complete (button shows "✓ Applied!")
- Some animations queue messages, others replace immediately
- Try clicking after animation entrance completes (~2-3 seconds)

### Security

Dynamic text uses **origin-validated postMessage** for secure cross-iframe communication:
- Gallery only sends messages with explicit origin (no wildcard `'*'`)
- Animations validate `event.origin` before processing messages
- Allowed origins: same origin + localhost dev servers
- Prevents malicious sites from injecting text into animations

See [Security Documentation](SECURITY.md) for more details. *(Optional: create SECURITY.md)*

### Performance

**Typical timings** (on modern hardware):
- Font loading: < 100ms (cached after first load)
- Path generation: < 50ms (for 1-10 words)
- Particle sampling: < 100ms
- Circle packing: 100-200ms
- Flubber interpolation: < 50ms

**Large text** (> 20 words) may experience:
- Slower generation times (200-500ms)
- Reduced frame rate during animation
- Increased memory usage

**Recommendations**:
- Keep text short (1-10 words) for best performance
- Avoid rapid clicking of "Generate" button
- Close unused animation cards to free resources

### Testing

See [TESTING.md](TESTING.md) for information about:
- Running unit tests
- Running E2E tests
